<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kampala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kampala is the capital and largest city of Uganda, near the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a>. It grew around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengo">Mengo</a>, the capital of the kabakas of Buganda, and the hill of Old Kampala, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> built a fort for the Imperial British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> Company in 1890. It replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entebbe">Entebbe</a> as the capital at independence in 1962 and is the seat of Buganda's royal palace and parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kampala.jpg" alt="Kampala" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chapelle musa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urban_Rising,_KAMPALA,_Uganda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
